  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "beat-01",
      "paragraph": 1,
      "text": "Booking confirmed. But the saved phone is wrong. An AI fix needs more than a convincing answer.",
      "file": "beat-01.wav",
      "start_seconds": 0.0,
      "end_seconds": 7.6,
      "audio_samples": 182400,
      "sample_rate": 24000,
      "generation_seconds": 16.098,
      "sha256": "7e8bc92632cd963040362d2d03218604c273c072d582d414dac36f512f1f8c15"
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-02",
      "paragraph": 2,
      "text": "AccessFinish connects a proposed code change to your review, approval of that exact patch, and independent execution evidence.",
      "file": "beat-02.wav",
      "start_seconds": 7.78,
      "end_seconds": 16.34,
      "audio_samples": 205440,
      "sample_rate": 24000,
      "generation_seconds": 17.404,
      "sha256": "8ef719762cd9b743f8982803094e824ada9194003e7758edb1b4074f0b6a21df"
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-03",
      "paragraph": 3,
      "text": "For our second case, we deliberately seeded a phone serialization fault. One new NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super proposal, through Nebius Token Factory, repaired it with an operator-supplied diagnosis.",
      "file": "beat-03.wav",
      "start_seconds": 16.52,
      "end_seconds": 29.88,
      "audio_samples": 320640,
      "sample_rate": 24000,
      "generation_seconds": 29.322,
      "sha256": "d027e2c222563d9e86ca42e5fc10341ce5174dc17511bbf85f1dd009760bb29e"
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-04",
      "paragraph": 4,
      "text": "The entered phone was saved exactly, including leading zeroes, and reopened in a fresh browser. A different phone also passed the regression control.",
      "file": "beat-04.wav",
      "start_seconds": 30.06,
      "end_seconds": 40.22,
      "audio_samples": 243840,
      "sample_rate": 24000,
      "generation_seconds": 23.934,
      "sha256": "75ab2a8994507173adab5d166b1eb8d6e98a9a1a3b45e90c11c2edefe3bd26ef"
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-05",
      "paragraph": 5,
      "text": "A hardcoded reference repair passed the first booking, then failed the different-phone check. Both failures and successes remain visible.",
      "file": "beat-05.wav",
      "start_seconds": 40.4,
      "end_seconds": 49.12,
      "audio_samples": 209280,
      "sample_rate": 24000,
      "generation_seconds": 18.847,
      "sha256": "7a8bef5da7b17f698030f4a5aba4b2b9b46e60f499742a8c230222418795bbf0"
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-06",
      "paragraph": 6,
      "text": "We compared AccessFinish with a conventional test-only workflow using the same build, browser, database reader, reopen, and regression checks.",
      "file": "beat-06.wav",
      "start_seconds": 49.3,
      "end_seconds": 59.38,
      "audio_samples": 241920,
      "sample_rate": 24000,
      "generation_seconds": 20.655,
      "sha256": "954db3badbddb565641509892c536c379fdd6864b59a6ba0c3ea16e53b3aa21e"
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-07",
      "paragraph": 7,
      "text": "Across six paired variants and twelve isolated executions, both workflows agreed on every correctness outcome. The new Nemotron proposal also passed both workflows in two additional replays.",
      "file": "beat-07.wav",
      "start_seconds": 59.56,
      "end_seconds": 73.08,
      "audio_samples": 324480,
      "sample_rate": 24000,
      "generation_seconds": 28.866,
      "sha256": "83ddbe948b6ad7c97ccccac505919d572017479334d6a23976bbe074e17a406e"
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-08",
      "paragraph": 8,
      "text": "The difference is the repair decision. AccessFinish rejected missing and stale approvals, then attached each accepted approval to its exact source, patch, and run.",
      "file": "beat-08.wav",
      "start_seconds": 73.26,
      "end_seconds": 85.9,
      "audio_samples": 303360,
      "sample_rate": 24000,
      "generation_seconds": 26.233,
      "sha256": "7a2e28a46b995fa6955576d11808f697254c58c2a4591d17ad5145705118cd3d"
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-09",
      "paragraph": 9,
      "text": "The original keyboard date case remains separate: two complete passes from five guided model attempts.",
      "file": "beat-09.wav",
      "start_seconds": 86.08,
      "end_seconds": 92.72,
      "audio_samples": 159360,
      "sample_rate": 24000,
      "generation_seconds": 14.024,
      "sha256": "75a0a25f455ecc5fe1aefdcbaff3c6c6ced09980102835b8c13825c6efc07b45"
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-10",
      "paragraph": 10,
      "text": "These are two exposed cases in one application, including one deliberately seeded fault. They do not establish general repair accuracy or time savings.",
      "file": "beat-10.wav",
      "start_seconds": 92.9,
      "end_seconds": 103.62,
      "audio_samples": 257280,
      "sample_rate": 24000,
      "generation_seconds": 22.184,
      "sha256": "f1797ff46826b73bf6d3ccfd0f80c10253eebda6a7901809f4f11123b75b96db"
    },
    {
      "id": "beat-11",
      "paragraph": 11,
      "text": "AccessFinish. Review the change. Know which repair you can accept.",
      "file": "beat-11.wav",
      "start_seconds": 103.8,
